{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "f77b3731-f87c-4dd9-822a-4509de8cb5eb"/*PoseLandmarkDetectionExample*/,
  "Description": "Detects full-body poses in a live camera image and shows the built-in debug view: the camera frame with all 33 landmarks of every detected person.\n\nTurn [Debug] off to get the clean camera image on [OutputTexture]. The poses are provided as data: [PointBuffer] holds 33 points per person in centered image coordinates (Y up, roughly -1..1), each point carrying its landmark index (0 = nose, 11/12 = shoulders, 23/24 = hips) in F1. [WorldLandmarksBuffer] holds metric world-space landmarks, [PoseCount] the number of people, and [SegmentationMask] a mask of the detected persons (only when the pose model emits masks - the bundled one does not).\n\n[CorrectAspectRatio] keeps positions aligned with non-square camera images.",
  "InputUis": [],
  "SymbolChildUis": [
